\section*{A gap in the open spin-one chain with fixed same-sign boundary fields}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a proof in the selected manuscript. Odd open spin-one chains with endpoint field $3/5$ are claimed to have gap above $\log(10)/392$ from the stated length onward, with selected infinite-volume index $-1$.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Result 1.} For a spin-one open chain on \(2L+1\) sites, with coupling one and equal endpoint fields, set
\[
 H_L(h)=\sum_{j=-L}^{L-1}\boldsymbol S_j\cdot\boldsymbol S_{j+1}
 -h(S_{-L}^z+S_L^z),\qquad\sum_a(S^a)^2=2I.
\]
Let \(E_0\le E_1\) be its two lowest eigenvalues counting multiplicity. At the fixed field \(h=3/5\), the claimed bound is
\[
 E_1(L,3/5)-E_0(L,3/5)>\frac{\log10}{392}\qquad(L\ge960).
\]
No endpoint-to-endpoint bond is included.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Endpoint fields enter boundary vectors of a spatial transfer operator. Periodic concentration estimates are extended to boundary-weighted moments, and finite initialization with quadratic improvement gives the uniform gap; the index conclusion then uses the cited index theorem.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Odd open spin-one chains with endpoint field $3/5$ are claimed to have gap above $\log(10)/392$ from the stated length onward, with selected infinite-volume index $-1$. The question retains these same parameters and conventions. Within these assumptions, this is a claimed affirmative answer to the stated question.

